		####################################################################
		### RETIRED - THE CLAIM LIST OF THE AI LETTER.  V13 USER ITEM 1.
		###
		### The granted claim was built, shipped and played TWICE (a single-object
		### picker, then this multi-select), then CONSIDERED AND WITHDRAWN FOR AN
		### INDEFINITE PERIOD. A DESIGN REFUSAL, NOT A BUG FIX: vanilla gates the
		### MANUFACTURE of claims behind a LEARNING investment - they come from the
		### Court Chaplain's council task (task_fabricate_claim,
		### GAME\common\council_tasks\00_court_chaplain_tasks.txt:1088) with the
		### outcome keyed to learning (:1120, :1126, :1132). Buying a finished claim
		### at the table short-circuits the whole investment.
		###
		### THE ROW GOES BECAUSE ITS WRITER GOES, which is this block's invariant:
		### archetype A11, the letter that sold paper claims, was the only AI path
		### that filled tnt_sel_claim_r, and it retires with the term. A live group
		### here would read as a missing writer rather than as a retired term.
		###
		### tnt_count_sel_claim_r_value, this group's `visible`, is one of the two
		### values kept DEFINED but gutted to 0 because five loc keys name it -
		### tnt_ai_offer_row_claim_r among them, and that key stays defined too (the
		### key set is pinned at 553 and an undefined key prints raw).
		### Nothing is deleted; do not re-enable one half. ARCHETYPE INDEX 11 IS
		### RETIRED and must never be reused.
		### Full tombstone: TOMBSTONE C in gui\tnt_diplomacy_window.gui, and
		### common\scripted_effects\tnt_32_apply.txt.
		####################################################################
